{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RSZIsoformalInterface"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane.not_integralSlopeSetting_bindingKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane.not_integralSlopeSetting_bindingKernel","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingNoAlienPlane.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**The binding kernel cannot satisfy RSZ §3.3's standing hypotheses.**\n\n§3.3 presupposes at least two slopes (the level `μ₂ − μ₁` is a *binary*\noperation).  `L_K` has one.  So the section whose machinery would produce a\nStokes multiplier does not apply to it — mechanically, not by inspection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane.isoformalDim_two_slope_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane.isoformalDim_two_slope_pos","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingNoAlienPlane.lean#L98-L108","doc":"**The vanishing above is a fact about `L_K`, not about the formula.**\n\nAt two slopes with positive ranks the isoformal dimension is strictly positive.\nSo `bindingKernel_isoformalDim_eq_zero` is not vacuous: it says the binding\nkernel has *one* slope, and it is exactly that one-slope-ness — purity — that\nempties the Stokes plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane.bindingKernel_isoformalDim_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingNoAlienPlane.bindingKernel_isoformalDim_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingNoAlienPlane.lean#L85-L96","doc":"**The binding kernel's `∞` has no local isoformal moduli.**\n\n`L_K = (q²x−1)σ² − (q−1)σ − (q−1)` is pure isoclinic at `∞` with Newton data\n`(r, d) = (2, 1)` — one edge, rank `2`, slope `½`\n(`QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion`).  One slope means no pairs\n`i < j` in RSZ Thm 3.3.5's sum, so the isoformal space is a point.\n\nThere is therefore no local q-Stokes multiplier at the binding kernel's `∞` to\nextract, and no q-alien derivation acting there. ","signatureChunk":0}]}